Important

A password reset should not be performed before verifying the user's identity and authorization.

8. Locked vs Disabled Account
Locked Account

A locked account is temporarily prevented from authenticating.

A common cause is repeated failed login attempts triggering the organization's account-lockout policy.

Disabled Account

A disabled account still exists in Active Directory but has been intentionally disabled by an administrator or policy.

Comparison
Locked
↓
Temporary authentication restriction

Disabled
↓
Account intentionally disabled

Deleted
↓
Account removed from Active Directory
Help Desk Approach

If an account is locked:

Verify the user's identity.
Check account status.
Unlock the account if authorized.
Investigate repeated lockouts if necessary.
Verify the user's login.
Document the resolution.
